# C8 reduced TS: OptTS with the host frozen via the QM/MM active region.
#
# Seed: geometry_b973c-xtb/ts/job.xyz -- the verified r2SCAN-3c TS (H135
# transferring, C129...O136 1.820) with its host already relaxed at B97-3c in
# step 1. r2SCAN-3c and B97-3c are both 3c composite methods and differ little
# geometrically, so the QM region already sits in the B97-3c saddle's catchment
# and OptTS only refines it and pins the imaginary mode.
#
# ActiveAtoms + ExtendActiveRegion no hold the 120-atom host and move only the
# 17 QM atoms. See the 2026-09-21 COMPUTATIONAL.md entry for why %geom Cartesian
# constraints were the wrong mechanism here (ORCA still carried all 137 atoms in
# a redundant-internal set, so convergence could never be met).
#
# Calc_Hess true: OptTS needs the exact Hessian to find and follow the imaginary
# mode. A separate NumFreq on the result gives the one-imaginary-mode verdict.
! QM/XTB B97-3c ddCOSMO(Water) OptTS TightSCF

%QMMM
QMATOMS
	{61 64 120 121 122 124 125 126 128 129 130 131 132 133 134 135 136}
END
ActiveAtoms
	{61 64 120 121 122 124 125 126 128 129 130 131 132 133 134 135 136}
END
ExtendActiveRegion no
Charge_total 0
Mult_total 1
AutoFF_QM2_Method GFNFF
END

%geom
  Calc_Hess true
end

%output jsonpropfile true end

%maxcore 4000

%pal
   nprocs 8
end

* xyzfile 0 1 job.xyz
